; AVP: Vendor-Specific-Application-Id
; Command: MT-Forward-Short-Message-Answer
; Section: 6.3.2.2
; Page: 47
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.3.0
"The Vendor-Specific-Application-Id AVP shall not be included in any command sent by Diameter nodes supporting applications defined in this specification."
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.338.dadx#sc-address-tbcd)
; AVP: SC-Address
; Section: 6.3.3.2
; Page: 51
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.3.0
"The SC-Address AVP is of type OctetString and it shall contain the E.164 number of the SMS-SC or MTC-IWF, in international number format as described in ITU-T Recommendation E.164 [13] and encoded as a TBCD-string."
"This AVP shall not include leading indicators for the nature of address and the numbering plan; it shall contain only the TBCD-encoded digits of the address."
    encoding e164-tbcd


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.338.dadx#sm-rp-ui-tpdu)
; AVP: SM-RP-UI
; Section: 6.3.3.3
; Page: 51
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.3.0
"The SM-RP-UI is of type OctetString and it shall contain a short message transfer protocol data unit (TPDU) which is defined in 3GPP TS 23.040 [3] and represents the user data field carried by the short message service relay sub-layer protocol."
    encoding element TS23.040 9.2.2 "TPDU"
"Its maximum length is of 200 octets."
    length *..200 octets


; Type: Value Table
; AVP: TFR-Flags
; Kind: bits
; Section: 6.3.3.4
; Table: 6.3.3.4/1
; Page: 51
More-Messages-To-Send = 0


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.338.dadx#tfr-flags-undefined-bits)
; AVP: TFR-Flags
; Section: 6.3.3.4
; Table: 6.3.3.4/1
; Page: 51
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.3.0
"NOTE 1: Bits not defined in this table shall be cleared by the sending entity and discarded by the receiving entity."
    bits only 0


; Type: Grouped AVP
; Name: SM-Delivery-Failure-Cause
; Section: 6.3.3.5
; Page: 52
SM-Delivery-Failure-Cause ::= < AVP header: 3303 10415 >
        { SM-Enumerated-Delivery-Failure-Cause }
        [ SM-Diagnostic-Info ]
      * [ AVP ]


; Type: Enumerated AVP
; Name: SM-Enumerated-Delivery-Failure-Cause
; Section: 6.3.3.6
; Page: 52
SM-Enumerated-Delivery-Failure-Cause ::= < Enumerated AVP header: 3304 10415 >
        MEMORY_CAPACITY_EXCEEDED  = 0
        EQUIPMENT_PROTOCOL_ERROR  = 1
        EQUIPMENT_NOT_SM-EQUIPPED = 2
        UNKNOWN_SERVICE_CENTRE    = 3
        SC-CONGESTION             = 4
        INVALID_SME-ADDRESS       = 5
        USER_NOT_SC-USER          = 6


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.338.dadx#sgd-feature-list-id)
; AVP: Feature-List-ID
; Section: 6.3.3.8
; Page: 52
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.3.0
"For this release, the Feature-List-ID AVP value shall be set to 1."
    range 1


; Type: Value Table
; AVP: OFR-Flags
; Kind: bits
; Section: 6.3.3.12
; Table: 6.3.3.12/1
; Page: 53
"S6a/S6d-Indicator" = 0


; Type: Grouped AVP
; Name: SMSMI-Correlation-ID
; Section: 6.3.3.13
; Page: 53
SMSMI-Correlation-ID ::= < AVP header: 3324 10415 > ;; corrected: (TS29.338.py#smsmi-correlation-id-name) ;; corrected: (TS29.338.py#smsmi-correlation-id-code)
        [ HSS-ID ]
        [ Originating-SIP-URI ]
        [ Destination-SIP-URI ]
      * [ AVP ]


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.338.dadx#hss-id-composition)
; AVP: HSS-ID
; Section: 6.3.3.14
; Page: 53
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.3.0
"The definition and the composition of the HSS-ID are specified in 3GPP TS 23.003 [16]."
    encoding element TS23.003 5.3 "HSS-ID"


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.338.dadx#sms-gmsc-address-tbcd)
; AVP: SMS-GMSC-Address
; Section: 6.3.3.19
; Page: 54
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.3.0
"The SMS-GMSC-Address AVP is of type OctetString and it shall contain the E.164 number of the SMS-GMSC or SMS Router, in international number format as described in ITU-T Recommendation E.164 [13] and encoded as a TBCD-string."
"This AVP shall not include leading indicators for the nature of address and the numbering plan; it shall contain only the TBCD-encoded digits of the address."
    encoding e164-tbcd


